      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="684674195">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP184 - Brooks&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for another day of capping and caching with OBA, this time we went east!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; This may have been an easy find, but it sure isn't easy to read! What a battered up cap! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_sad.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; A lady stopped to ask what we were up to, as there had been people there stealing rocks not too long ago. (I don't know where from, since I didn't see any rocks, but maybe I was just too focussed on the cap!) &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_wink.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684654987">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP184 - Brooks - we were stopped by the nearby land owner, she was fine with us taking pictures of the cap, but she said she chased away people stealing rocks the other day ... odd that.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
